.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt CD9660 5
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm cd9660
.Nd ISO 9660 file system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm mount
.Fl t Cm cd9660
.Op Fl o Cm norrip , Ns Cm nojoliet
.Ar special node
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
file system reads ISO 9660 volumes: CDs, DVDs and the images written to them or
to USB sticks, such as OxideBSD's install medium.
It is always read-only: a mount asked for read-write is made read-only, and
.Nm mount Fl u Fl w
fails with
.Er EROFS .
.Pp
Names and attributes come from the first of these the volume has:
.Bl -tag -width "Rock Ridge"
.It Rock Ridge
POSIX names, permissions, owners, link counts, times and symbolic links, as
.Xr xorriso 1
writes them; directories nested deeper than ISO 9660 allows, which Rock Ridge
relocates, appear where they belong.
.It Joliet
Unicode names of up to 64 characters.
.It ISO 9660
Names of the
.Dq 8.3
form, shown in lower case without their version
.Pq Dq \&;1 .
.El
.Pp
Without Rock Ridge every file belongs to root, with permissions 0555, and the
recording time stands in for every time.
.Pp
The options:
.Bl -tag -width nojoliet
.It Cm norrip
Ignore Rock Ridge
.Pq Xr mount_cd9660 8 Fl r on Fx .
.It Cm nojoliet
Ignore Joliet
.Pq Fl j on Fx .
.El
.Pp
A file's inode number is where its directory record is on the volume (a
directory's, where its contents start), as on
.Fx .
.Pp
Only the first session of a multi-session disc is read.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/dev/ide0"
.It Pa /dev/ide0
an IDE CD drive; its kind is in
.Va kern.disk.ide0.kind
.Pq Xr sysctl 8 .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fstab 5 ,
.Xr msdosfs 5 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
file system first appeared in
.Bx 4.4 .
OxideBSD's is its own, written for it.
.Sh BUGS
Files of more than one extent (over 4 GiB) are read, but ISO 9660's extended
attribute records, interleaved files and zisofs compression are not.
